  "design": "One coarse cell with four equal-mass balanced label pairs per block. In the high state the added feature agrees with three pairs and flips one. The low state reverses those outcomes. Each state has marginal probability one half, so each record's added feature is marginally fair given the cohort. The frozen rule predicts the added feature. Scores are one-quarter or three-quarters of the mutable block mass. False certification means a strictly positive lower bound.",
  "assumptions": {
    "adjacent_pairs": "Independent successive pairs of blocks with correlation rho inside each pair. An unpaired final block is independent.",
    "persistent_markov": "Stationary symmetric two-state Markov chain with lag-one correlation rho and lag-two correlation rho squared.",
    "range": "[0, 1 / blocks] from the mutable block mass",
    "method_scope": "At rho=0 all methods have their assumed independence. For adjacent pairs, the parity methods remain valid at all rho values.",
    "calculation": "Exact recursion over the last state and the number of high scores"
  },
